  "updateinfo_id": "ALSA-2026:80694",
  "description": "Mozilla Thunderbird is a standalone mail and newsgroup client.  \n\nSecurity Fix(es):  \n\n  * firefox: thunderbird: Use-after-free in the Graphics: Canvas2D component (CVE-2026-100832)\n  * firefox: Use-after-free in the Layout: Text and Fonts component (CVE-2026-100784)\n  * firefox: thunderbird: Privilege escalation in the DLL Services component (CVE-2026-100801)\n  * firefox: thunderbird: Sandbox escape due to incorrect boundary conditions in the Internationalization component (CVE-2026-100794)\n  * firefox: thunderbird: Privilege escalation in the Address Bar component (CVE-2026-100820)\n  * firefox: thunderbird: Use-after-free in the Graphics: Canvas2D component (CVE-2026-100777)\n  * firefox: thunderbird: Information disclosure in the Networking: JAR component (CVE-2026-100766)\n  * firefox: thunderbird: Use-after-free in the XSLT component (CVE-2026-100779)\n  * firefox: thunderbird: Privilege escalation in the DOM: Service Workers component (CVE-2026-100807)\n  * firefox: thunderbird: JIT miscompilation in the JavaScript: WebAssembly component (CVE-2026-100792)\n  * firefox: Privilege escalation due to use-after-free in the Graphics: WebRender component (CVE-2026-100797)\n  * firefox: thunderbird: Sandbox escape due to incorrect boundary conditions in the XPCOM component (CVE-2026-100819)\n  * firefox: thunderbird: Use-after-free in the JavaScript: WebAssembly component (CVE-2026-100776)\n  * firefox: thunderbird: Use-after-free in the Widget component (CVE-2026-100757)\n  * firefox: Sandbox escape due to use-after-free in the Graphics component (CVE-2026-100786)\n  * firefox: thunderbird: Information disclosure in the Networking component (CVE-2026-96869)\n  * firefox: Sandbox escape due to use-after-free in the DOM: Content Processes component (CVE-2026-100770)\n  * firefox: thunderbird: Use-after-free in the JavaScript: WebAssembly component (CVE-2026-100769)\n  * firefox: Use-after-free in the DOM: Core \u0026 HTML component (CVE-2026-100791)\n  * firefox: thunderbird: Sandbox escape due to use-after-free in the Widget: Gtk component (CVE-2026-100818)\n  * firefox: thunderbird: Privilege escalation due to incorrect boundary conditions in the Graphics component (CVE-2026-100782)\n  * firefox: firefox: Sandbox escape via use-after-free in DOM component (CVE-2026-100811)\n  * firefox: thunderbird: Use-after-free in the DOM: Core \u0026 HTML component (CVE-2026-100772)\n  * firefox: thunderbird: Uninitialized memory in the Storage: Quota Manager component (CVE-2026-100759)\n  * firefox: Sandbox escape due to use-after-free in the DOM: Core \u0026 HTML component (CVE-2026-100778)\n  * firefox: thunderbird: Sandbox escape in the DOM: Navigation component (CVE-2026-100758)\n  * firefox: thunderbird: Sandbox escape in the Graphics component (CVE-2026-100775)\n  * firefox: thunderbird: Sandbox escape due to incorrect boundary conditions in the Graphics: WebRender component (CVE-2026-100781)\n  * firefox: Use-after-free in the DOM: Core \u0026 HTML component (CVE-2026-100774)\n  * firefox: thunderbird: Same-origin policy bypass in the WebExtensions component (CVE-2026-100803)\n  * firefox: thunderbird: Use-after-free in the Graphics: Canvas2D component (CVE-2026-100789)\n  * firefox: thunderbird: Use-after-free in the DOM: Core \u0026 HTML component (CVE-2026-100785)\n  * firefox: thunderbird: Site isolation issue in the Panning and Zooming component (CVE-2026-100821)\n  * firefox: thunderbird: Invalid pointer in the JavaScript: WebAssembly component (CVE-2026-100788)\n  * firefox: thunderbird: Undefined behavior in the DOM: Streams component (CVE-2026-100771)\n  * firefox: Sandbox escape due to use-after-free in the DOM: Content Processes component (CVE-2026-100762)\n  * firefox: thunderbird: Use-after-free in the XSLT component (CVE-2026-100790)\n  * firefox: thunderbird: Use-after-free in the Storage: IndexedDB component (CVE-2026-100773)\n  * firefox: thunderbird: Use-after-free in the DOM: Core \u0026 HTML component (CVE-2026-100780)\n  * firefox: thunderbird: Use-after-free in the Networking: Cache component (CVE-2026-100767)\n  * firefox: thunderbird: Incorrect boundary conditions in the Audio/Video: Playback component (CVE-2026-100756)\n  * firefox: thunderbird: Uninitialized memory in the Audio/Video component (CVE-2026-100783)\n\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n",
